   "suspension arm geometry (pivot, length), steering offset": "estimate: not published; pivots under the chassis and a 0.15 m steering offset chosen so that the nominal track is 1.3 m, the wheelbase 1.0 m and +/-40 deg of arm travel changes ride height and track, as the PSJ paper describes",
   "body 1.44 x 1.48 x 0.58 m with 0.07 m chamfered vertical and top edges, belly 0.72 m above ground, a 1.20 x 0.40 x 0.15 m keel under it carrying the suspension actuators": "estimate: proportions read from NASA photos and renders of the rover; sized so that with the arrays it fills the 1.5 m published body width and 1.7 m envelope, and the 0.5 m wheels stay clear of it at +/-50 deg steering",
   "front face white/silver (MLI and radiator), not an array; MLI on the front and belly": "estimate: from NASA photos of the rover (the sources list arrays on three sides only)",
   "solar array panels 1.26 x 0.50 m (sides), 1.30 x 0.50 m (aft), on the flat body faces": "estimate: panel area not found; each panel covers the flat part of its body face",
   "radiator 0.92 x 1.24 m on the aft two thirds of the deck, raised rim around the deck": "estimate: not found",
