   "high-gain dish diameter 0.40 m, pointing low (Earth near the horizon at the pole)": "estimate: diameter not found",
   "TRIDENT position: tower at the front face, right of centre (y = -0.18 m), footpad 0.36 m above ground, rail top about 1.66 m": "estimate: placement read from NASA renders and integration photos (no published coordinates); the published facts are the belly integration and the 1 m stroke. The bay inside the body is not modelled: the stowed rail stands on the front face and the auger reaches below the belly",
   "TRIDENT rail 1.30 m, auger 25 mm, flight 42 mm, footpad 0.12 m": "estimate: sized for the 1 m stroke; not published",
   "NSS box 0.12 x 0.30 x 0.20 m low on the front face; NIRVSS on the keel front near the drill; MSolo under the keel": "estimate: sizes not found; positions follow the published 'front' and 'under the rover'",
   "mass split (per corner: wheel+drive 12 kg, steering 8 kg, arm 10 kg; chassis 330 kg, of which drill 19.8 kg)": "estimate: only the total (and the < 20 kg drill) is published; the split sets the centre of mass and inertia computed from the CAD",
   "drive actuator torque limit 80 N m, wheel speed limit 2.5 rad/s": "estimate: not published; 80 N m exceeds the soil torque of the wheel at 90 % slip under the static lunar load on GRC-1, so traction, not the motor, limits climbing",
